      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Four days at 750 records per day account for the remaining 3,000." data-hint="Multiply the documented daily rate by Tuesday through Friday." data-fix="Four times 750 equals the remaining 3,000 records."><p class="quiz-question">2. What arithmetic supports the Friday completion forecast?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Four days at 750 records per day account for the remaining 3,000.">Four days at 750 records per day account for the remaining 3,000.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="One day at 5,400 records guarantees every future result.">One day at 5,400 records guarantees every future result.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Eight days at twelve images equal the archive total.">Eight days at twelve images equal the archive total.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The completion forecast depends on the rate continuing with no outage." data-hint="Find the explicit if-condition in the forecast." data-fix="The forecast depends on the 750-record rate continuing with no outage."><p class="quiz-question">3. What prevents the Future Perfect statement from being a guarantee?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The completion forecast depends on the rate continuing with no outage.">The completion forecast depends on the rate continuing with no outage.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Future Perfect grammar always proves a future fact.">Future Perfect grammar always proves a future fact.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The records were already incomplete after Friday.">The records were already incomplete after Friday.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Two auditors will be reviewing a 200-record sample." data-hint="Use the 1:30 to 3:00 audit window and the 2:00 camera." data-fix="At 2:00, two auditors will be reviewing a 200-record sample."><p class="quiz-question">4. What activity is expected at 2:00 Friday?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Two auditors will be reviewing a 200-record sample.">Two auditors will be reviewing a 200-record sample.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The entire archive will begin after 4:30.">The entire archive will begin after 4:30.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Seven specialists will have become records.">Seven specialists will have become records.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The sample review is expected to be complete by 4:30." data-hint="The activity surrounds 2:00, but its report deadline is later." data-fix="The sample review is expected to be complete by the 4:30 report deadline."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which result is expected by 4:30?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The sample review is expected to be complete by 4:30.">The sample review is expected to be complete by 4:30.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The sample review is expected to begin after 4:30.">The sample review is expected to begin after 4:30.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The March 29 start will become a future sample.">The March 29 start will become a future sample.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Six weeks of migration work will have accumulated by Friday evening." data-hint="Connect the March 29 start to the May 10 future point." data-fix="Six weeks of migration work will have accumulated by Friday evening."><p class="quiz-question">6. What does the Future Perfect Continuous establish?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Six weeks of migration work will have accumulated by Friday evening.">Six weeks of migration work will have accumulated by Friday evening.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The form alone proves every task stops exactly at 5:00.">The form alone proves every task stops exactly at 5:00.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The migration began six weeks after Friday.">The migration began six weeks after Friday.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Five images are expected complete and seven are expected still in restoration." data-hint="Keep the completed quantity and in-progress quantity together." data-fix="Five images are expected complete; seven are expected still in restoration."><p class="quiz-question">7. What mixed result-and-process forecast applies to the twelve images?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Five images are expected complete and seven are expected still in restoration.">Five images are expected complete and seven are expected still in restoration.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All twelve images are guaranteed complete on Monday.">All twelve images are guaranteed complete on Monday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Seven images are complete and five specialists are damaged.">Seven images are complete and five specialists are damaged.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The file does not guarantee the rate, rule out an outage, or assign personal responsibility for a changed forecast." data-hint="Choose all three explicit limits together." data-fix="The rate, outage status, and individual responsibility remain limited by the evidence."><p class="quiz-question">8. Which close reports the forecast responsibly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The file does not guarantee the rate, rule out an outage, or assign personal responsibility for a changed forecast.">The file does not guarantee the rate, rule out an outage, or assign personal responsibility for a changed forecast.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Future Perfect proves the team will finish, so one person is responsible for any difference.">Future Perfect proves the team will finish, so one person is responsible for any difference.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because uncertainty exists, no forecast or staffing decision is possible.">Because uncertainty exists, no forecast or staffing decision is possible.</button></div></div>
    </div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
