  <h2>Notice and repair the broken viewpoint</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="completed" data-hint="Future Perfect needs base have between will and the participle." data-fix="By Friday, the team will have completed the checks." data-why="Will is followed by base have, which is followed by the lexical participle completed." data-success-message="Correct. The completion chain now contains will, have, and the participle."><h3>Repair 1: missing perfect auxiliary</h3><p>Tap the participle before which <span class="ex">have</span> is missing.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="by">By Friday</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="team">the team</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="will">will</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="completed">completed the checks.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="be" data-hint="Measured process duration up to June needs have been before -ing." data-fix="By June, she will have been working here for five years." data-why="Future Continuous places an activity around a point; Future Perfect Continuous measures its accumulated duration." data-success-message="Correct. Have been now connects the earlier start to the June checkpoint."><h3>Repair 2: duration, not just activity then</h3><p>Tap the auxiliary that leaves the five-year duration incomplete.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="june">By June</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">she will</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="be">be working</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="years">here for five years.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="will" data-hint="The future meaning belongs to the main clause; use a present form after when." data-fix="When the audit ends, we will publish the report." data-why="A future time clause normally uses Present Simple, while the main clause carries the future form." data-success-message="Correct. The when-clause now uses Present Simple without losing future meaning."><h3>Repair 3: future time clause</h3><p>Tap the unnecessary future auxiliary inside the time clause.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="when">When the audit</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="will">will end</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we">we will publish</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="report">the report.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="been" data-hint="The records receive the completed verification, so the passive requires been before the participle." data-fix="All 8,400 records will have been verified by Friday." data-why="Future Perfect passive is will have been plus participle; without been, the affected records appear to perform the action." data-success-message="Correct. Passive been restores the receiving role of the records."><h3>Repair 4: passive result</h3><p>Tap the position where the passive layer is missing.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="records">All 8,400 records</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="will">will have</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="been">verified</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="friday">by Friday.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>

